This is an existing software project with human-controlled source control.

SOURCE CONTROL IS USER-CONTROLLED:
- Never initialize or recreate the Git repository.
- Never rewrite Git history.
- Never force-push.
- Never rebase or reset branches.
- Never delete, rename, or replace branches or tags.
- Never change the default branch.
- Never create an orphan branch or unrelated root history.
- Never commit or push unless the user explicitly requests that specific Git operation.
- Do not modify .gitignore except when explicitly requested.
- Application changes must preserve existing repository history.

DATA SAFETY:
- Convex is the authoritative game-state backend.
- Never substitute another database.
- Never manually modify files under convex/_generated/.
- All persistent game-state changes must go through explicit Convex mutations.
- Preserve event history and recoverability.

CHANGE DISCIPLINE:
- Make only changes necessary for the requested task.
- If asked only to inspect, diagnose, or analyze, make NO file changes.
- Do not perform additional cleanup, migration, refactoring, deployment, or architectural changes unless explicitly requested.
- If a blocker requires changing architecture or tooling, stop and explain the blocker before making that change.